      "title": "Invariant plural units embedded as counted nouns break native French agreement",
      "actual": [
        "reste 1 crédits",
        "utilisation de 1 requêtes",
        "reste 1,5 jetons"
      ],
      "rationale": "Avoiding adjective gender with utilisation de does not fix noun-number agreement. Current Intl fr selects one for 0, 1 and 1.5; ordinary singular one case is unambiguously malformed. This is a native language defect in the directly changed high-visibility amount phrases, not structural ICU failure.",
      "remediation": "Move invariant unit to a caption outside the counted-noun phrase, preserving value:number and unit:string; e.g. Solde ({unit}) : {value, number} / Utilisation ({unit}) : {value, number}. Or implement actual unit inflection with an explicitly agreed source contract; no wider contract change is required for the caption approach.",
      "counterfactual_probe": "Same actual relay formatter accepts alternate scratch map with unchanged params; all 0/1/2/1.5 credits/USD/tokens/requests render correctly as captions. No submitted file edited."
    }
